// The driver names build.ctx's directory to the build program in ASCII, so std's C
// getenv, which gives the ANSI code page's bytes on Windows, reads it as it is.
// `ctxc graph` runs the build program without building the executables, whose files needn't
// compile. ctxc's own directory for it is removed before and after: the runner clears those of
// `ctxc run` commands only.
//# remove {work:café}
//# $ ctxc graph café {dir}/graph-gen {dir}/graph.txt
//# stdout:
//| file café/src/main.ctx
//| struct Main @ café/src/main.ctx:1:1
//# remove {work:café}
